## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design an online, scalable PCA solution with drift detection and actionable alerts, not just theoretical knowledge. It combines streaming preprocessing, incremental factor analysis, and interpretable thresholds with real-time latency goals suitable for fintech dashboards.

## Key Concepts

- IncrementalPCA vs batch PCA
- Online imputation and scaling
- Drift detection via explained variance and loadings
- Latency budgeting in streaming analytics
- Interpretability via region-aware loadings

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: online PCA scaffold
class OnlinePCAProcessor {
  constructor(nComponents = 10) {
    this.pca = new IncrementalPCA(n_components: nComponents)
    this.scaler = new StandardScaler()
    this.driftThreshold = 0.15
  }

  processBatch(batch) {
    // Impute missing values with column means
    const imputed = this.imputeMissing(batch)
    const scaled = this.scaler.fitTransform(imputed)
    const components = this.pca.partialFit(scaled)
    return this.detectDrift(components)
  }
}

## Why This Is Asked
Real-time risk analytics require interpretable, robust dimensionality reduction under nonstationarity. This question tests algorithm design, drift handling, and production latency optimization.

## Key Concepts
- **Online Sparse PCA**: Incremental SVD with L1 penalty to enforce sparsity constraints
- **Drift Detection**: Monitor loadings divergence and reconstruction error for nonstationarity
- **Online Imputation**: Rolling window-based imputation with robust scaling
- **Latency Budgeting**: System-level timing allocation across pipeline stages
- **Evaluation**: Drift scenarios, end-to-end latency profiling, and interpretability validation

## Code Example
```javascript
class OnlineSparsePCA {
  constructor(k, maxNonZeros) {
    this.k = k;
    this.maxNonZeros = maxNonZeros;
    this.components = null;
    this.imputer = new RollingImputer();
    this.scaler = new RobustScaler();
    this.driftMonitor = new DriftMonitor();
  }

  update(x) {
    const t0 = Date.now();
    const xImputed = this.imputer.transform(x);
    const xScaled = this.scaler.transform(xImputed);

    this.components = this.incrementalSparseSVD(xScaled);

    this.driftMonitor.check(this.components, xScaled);

    return { latencies: { impute: t1-t0, scale: t2-t1, svd: t3-t2, total: Date.now()-t0 } };
  }
}
```

